   "what_the_market_was_braced_for": "Heading into the Q2 FY2027 print, the market expected Marvell to deliver roughly $2.71B in revenue (vs. company guidance of $2.70B +/- 5%) and non-GAAP EPS of about $0.92-$0.93 (guidance midpoint $0.93 +/- $0.05), i.e., a quarter in line with the high end of guidance after Q1's record $2.418B. For the forward quarter, consensus was set at ~$3.034B revenue and ~$1.07 non-GAAP EPS (GAAP ~$0.52). The stock had drifted down ~3.9% over the five sessions before the print, and headlines flagged a very large potential swing (~$20.8B market value) around the release, with the option-implied move not quantified in the available material. Investors were also focused on management's raised FY2027 (~$12B, ~45% YoY growth) and FY2028 (~$18B, ~50% YoY growth) revenue outlooks and the pace of ~$1B capacity prepayments to suppliers.",
